# Web Lesson LA14 -- classical Gram-Schmidt subtracts a projection.
# effects: none
# loops: 0
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * WHAT THIS SHOWS -- split a2 into its projection on q1 plus a perpendicular residual, then normalize it as q2.
# * PREREQUISITES -- LA06 projection, LA08 multiplication, LA13 conditioning.
# * SHAPES -- fixed A,Q:[row=3,column=2], R:[2,2], columns:[3].
# * EXECUTABLE CLAIM -- the checked fixture gives Q=[[1,0],[0,1],[0,0]] and R=[[1,1],[0,1]].
# * NUMERICAL CONTRACT -- exact fixture; positive R diagonal; CLI rejects residual norm <=1e-9.
# * BOUNDARY -- teaching classical Gram-Schmidt is not robust general QR.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
a1 = [1, 0, 0]
a2 = [1, 1, 0]
q1 = a1 / sqrt(dot(a1, a1))
r12 = dot(q1, a2)
projection = r12 * q1
residual = a2 - projection
q2 = residual / sqrt(dot(residual, residual))
q = transpose([q1, q2])
r = [[1, r12], [0, 1]]
a = transpose([a1, a2])
orthogonality_delta = matmul(transpose(q), q) - [[1, 0], [0, 1]]
reconstruction_delta = matmul(q, r) - a
orthogonality_error = sqrt(reduce_add(flatten(orthogonality_delta * orthogonality_delta)))
reconstruction_error = sqrt(reduce_add(flatten(reconstruction_delta * reconstruction_delta)))
near_q = [[0.5773502691896258, -0.40870137090696584], [0.5773502691896258, 0.8160431231482399], [0.5773502691896258, -0.40870137090696584]]  # admitted near-dependent result
near_r = [[1.7320508075688772, 1.732050807569455], [0, 0.00000000000081656941952928]]
near_a = [[1, 1], [1, 1.000000000001], [1, 1]]
near_orthogonality_delta = matmul(transpose(near_q), near_q) - [[1, 0], [0, 1]]
near_reconstruction_delta = matmul(near_q, near_r) - near_a
near_orthogonality_error = sqrt(reduce_add(flatten(near_orthogonality_delta * near_orthogonality_delta)))
near_reconstruction_error = sqrt(reduce_add(flatten(near_reconstruction_delta * near_reconstruction_delta)))
disp([a1, projection, residual, q2])  # visible subtraction trace
disp([q, r])  # fixed factors
disp([orthogonality_error, reconstruction_error])  # independent checks
disp([[reconstruction_error, orthogonality_error], [near_reconstruction_error, near_orthogonality_error]])  # exact versus near-dependent QR quality
# THE VISUAL -- projection subtraction turns overlapping columns into perpendicular Q directions.
def u:gram_schmidt_visual() { "Render the checked LA14 projection subtraction."; "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 980 470\" role=\"img\"><title>Classical Gram-Schmidt subtracts a projection</title><desc>The second column splits into a projection on the first unit column and a perpendicular residual, producing orthogonal Q columns.</desc><style>text{font-family:monospace;fill:#c0caf5}.p{fill:#24283b;stroke:#414868}.b{stroke:#7aa2f7}.pink{stroke:#f7768e}.gold{stroke:#e0af68}.g{stroke:#9ece6a}.v{fill:none;stroke-width:5}.ok{fill:#9ece6a}</style><rect width=\"980\" height=\"470\" fill=\"#1a1b26\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"32\">a2 = projection on q1 + perpendicular residual</text><rect class=\"p\" x=\"20\" y=\"60\" width=\"580\" height=\"330\"/><path class=\"v b\" d=\"M100 330L350 330\"/><path class=\"v pink\" d=\"M100 330L350 100\"/><path class=\"v gold\" d=\"M100 330L350 330\"/><path class=\"v g\" d=\"M350 330L350 100\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"360\">q1 / projection</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"220\">residual to q2</text><rect class=\"p\" x=\"630\" y=\"60\" width=\"330\" height=\"330\"/><text x=\"655\" y=\"110\">Q orthogonal columns</text><text x=\"655\" y=\"155\">R upper triangular</text><text class=\"ok\" x=\"655\" y=\"225\">||Q^TQ-I||F = 0</text><text class=\"ok\" x=\"655\" y=\"270\">||QR-A||F = 0</text><text x=\"655\" y=\"335\">max CLI shape [3,2]</text><text x=\"490\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dependent residual <= tolerance returns Err; bounded teaching code</text></svg>" }
visual = u:gram_schmidt_visual()  # bind once
visual  # render once
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * HOW TO READ THE RESULT -- gold is overlap removed from pink a2; green is the new perpendicular direction.
# * THE POINT -- orthogonal bases separate coordinates; exact reconstruction can coexist with degraded orthogonality, so Q^TQ and QR must be checked independently.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
